WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.970
Verse 7

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.970
The 
storm 
blasts

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:16.970
<i>Results.</i>

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:24.080
<i>There are those who believe the effort you
invest is more important than the results,</i>

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.220
<i>but that's incredibly stressful 
for both teachers and students.</i>

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.230
<i>Thoughts like "I tried" and "It was so hard"
can be blown away like the wind.</i>

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.340
<i>But "results" are a bedrock.</i>

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.750
<i>The foundation that holds your efforts in place.</i>

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.990
<i>And...</i>

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.640
<i>I didn't know the Shiranami Society 
had young up-and-comers like these.</i>

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.890
They're both from the team that 
won the High School Championship?

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:50.920
That's amazing!

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:51.990
I didn't know that.

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.080
Ayase Chihaya and Mashima Taichi...

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.470
Neither of them holds a title?

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.770
Will they be in the Master and Queen qualifiers?

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.640
Who's going to win their first title?

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.360
Winning the Yoshino Tournament 
would be a huge boost.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:08.110
<i>And... "results" will bring to you</i>

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.450
<i>a powerful tailwind.</i>

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.370
Feels like a team match, doesn't it?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.820
One of my teammates is gonna win!

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.370
It's nice to have a senpai, isn't it?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.890
I'd like to yield the match.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.840
<i>reminds me of the lonely 
dawns after we parted</i>

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:30.950
It will support you.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.710
Dr. Harada is weighing him down.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.620
Tasuki!

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.620
...show that your skill's 
what got you here!

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.040
You said you were going to win all
 your games today in that kimono, right?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.230
<i>We came this far</i>

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:55.610
<i>reminds me of the lonely 
dawns after we parted</i>

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.430
<i>with the support of so many people.</i>

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.600
Thank you very much.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.090
Thank you very much.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:11.320
<i>reminds me of the lonely 
dawns after we parted</i>

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.950
The Yoshino Tournament Class A winner is

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.200
Ayase Chihaya-san of the Shiranami Society.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.490
I didn't know there was a player like her.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.220
She's Harada-san's star pupil.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.360
She defeated the runner-up Master 
Takemura and former Queen Inokuma!

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.320
She has real talent.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.800
Damn, she's pretty!

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.460
She's a high school second-year? 
Same age as the Queen?

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.550
She's the favorite for
the East Japan qualifiers?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.560
Chihaya-chan!

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.540
That was just amazing.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:07.270
The Shiranami Society earned 
lots of points today.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.290
Oh, not at all.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.020
The Master and Queen qualifiers
 are going to be exciting!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.640
And she's such a pretty girl, too.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.480
A Queen match between her and Wakayama,
both the same age, would be huge.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.620
Especially since it'll be televised!

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.400
<i>I'm so glad she looks pretty to people
who don't know her well.</i>

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.430
<i>As exhausted as she is right now, 
she just looks like this to us.</i>

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:35.040
<b>Daze</b>

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.950
Who's going to be in the 
qualifiers two weeks from now?

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.400
The top contenders will be Yamamoto Yumi-san

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.910
and Urabe-san from Gunma.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.500
Inokuma-san's likely to be there, too. 
And from Saitama...

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.620
If we're talking about momentum,
today's winner, Ayase-san, is up there.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.630
I sure hope she wins.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:51.150
<i>Chihaya-chan... The class trip...</i>

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.810
<i>The winds are blowing toward her...</i>

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.900
<i>The winds of expectation.</i>

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.930
Ayase-san, if you want to be in 
the Queen qualifiers,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.410
we can discuss it.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.870
In the case of a very 
important official match,

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.420
you can always request 
an authorized absence.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:15.350
And the Queen match is the most 
important one of all for you, isn't it?

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.920
Think it over. I'll be here to help you.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.690
Chihaya!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.970
Chihaya! I'm sorry I ran late!

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.870
Wait, am I too late?

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.180
You're out of your hakama already?

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.520
I even rushed to buy a 
camera on my way here!

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.440
Oh... I guess I could just 
take a picture with my phone.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.730
But the shutter's so slow on mine,

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.330
and I panicked because you asked me
to come out of the blue!

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.450
So, how'd your match go?

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.660
Did you do the best you could?

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.750
Was it fun?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.460
<b>Huh?</b>

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:57.450
Huh?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.960
M-Mom... I...

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.380
I want to go on the class trip!

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.990
Huh? O-Of course you can go!

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.230
I want...

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.180
to be a high school teacher!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:20.520
What kind of teacher would I be
if I've never been on a class trip?!

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.060
I want to be Queen, too,

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:31.570
but I want to be an advisor and coach,
like Ms. Miyauchi and Coach Sakurazawa!

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:37.210
But today was this hakama's first match,

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.830
and I wanted to win!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:44.030
I did win!

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.950
Taichi and I worked so hard!

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:50.340
<i>I did it.</i>

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.250
<i>I did it.</i>

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:59.120
<i>I did the best I could.</i>

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.780
<i>And it was fun.</i>

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:19.080
Taichi.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.100
Something wrong?

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.140
Nah. I'm just tired.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.570
Chihaya was really good.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.340
She was.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.210
<i>Why aren't I the one</i>

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.070
<i>playing against Chihaya right now?</i>

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:55.890
Taichi...

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.210
You might laugh at this,

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.510
but for whatever reason,

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.930
I always thought of Chihaya as yours.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.530
You're the one who's been by her side
all these years, not me.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.250
What are you talking about, you weirdo?

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.140
I...

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:29.380
<i>...think of Chihaya as 
belonging to both of us.</i>

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.890
<i>There's not much difference 
between Arata and me.</i>

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.050
<i>Even though I'm closer to her...</i>

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.570
But Chihaya doesn't really belong 
to anyone, does she?

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:55.580
<i>October 20th.</i>

00:08:55.960 --> 00:09:00.050
<i>Mizusawa High School second-years' 
class trip, day one.</i>

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.580
<i>We're taking the bullet 
train from Tokyo to Kyoto.</i>

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.850
<b>Excited</b>

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.810
Are you sure this is what 
you want, Chi-chan?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.580
You had to miss the Queen qualifiers for this.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:09.980
Sure you won't regret it?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.790
There'll be another Queen match
 next year! I'll try then!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.740
<b>We'll have
exams next
 year...</b>

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:14.750
But this year...

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.730
I want to make memories with you!

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:26.250
Well, you're our class' captain, Horikawa.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:28.250
Class 2-9

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:30.020
Jeez, you guys keep following me 
around, even during free time!

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:32.940
Anyway, today we're all going 
to Kiyomizu Temple together.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:36.190
Tomorrow, after the Golden Pavilion, 
our free time will be at Shigureden.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:36.800
Okay!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.810
Class 2-5

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.350
What's wrong with Oe-san?

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.440
She said she couldn't sleep last night.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.810
She couldn't stop reading guides on kimono shops,
museums, shrines, and temples,

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:48.550
along with classical books 
for a sense of immersion.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:53.570
Class 2-1

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.860
Why the heck did you bring that?

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:51.630
Let me see it next!

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.110
Wait, is that...

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:55.440
Boys! Give it a rest!

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.140
Oh, crap! Hide it!

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.400
No, swallow it!

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.680
Ayase, Ayase!

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.150
Oh, it's you, Desktomu-kun!

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.790
You came all the way from Class 2-1's car?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.650
Want some candy?

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.400
Ayase, we need to talk.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.780
It seems like Mashima didn't show up.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:11.450
Huh?

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.430
The teacher said he called the 
school saying he had a fever.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:18.610
What?! Taichi's sick?! How could he
let that happen when we have our class trip?

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.220
Well...

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.040
Is his fever that bad?

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.660
I'll try to call him.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.070
Wait, Ayase...

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.780
Th-That's probably not what it is.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:28.590
Huh?

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.430
<i>Huh? Huh?!</i>

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:39.990
<i>Does that mean...</i>

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.020
<i>Taichi?!</i>

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.710
Kyoto Station

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.960
Kiyomizu Street

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.210
Kiyomizu Temple

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.470
Chi-chan, look! The fall 
colors are gorgeous!

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.460
I always knew Kiyomizu—

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:10.640
<i>Taichi...</i>

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:14.190
<i>Taichi didn't show up 
for his own class trip?</i>

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.380
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:18.810
<i>Don't tell me... Don't tell me he...</i>

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.900
What do you want, Chihaya? 
You're getting annoying.

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.240
You finally answered!

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.420
Taichi! What the heck are you doing?!

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.740
She's so loud...

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:30.000
I have a fever, so I'm resting. What else?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.410
<i>The fever thing was true?!</i>

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.650
Yes, it's true. 39 degrees Celsius.

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:34.490
<i>39 degrees?!</i>

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:35.830
That's bad!

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.850
<i>I've been to Kyoto lots of times, anyway.</i>

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.650
<i>So I figured I could just skip.</i>

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:42.770
Wow... Rich kid.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:45.110
<i>Is that all? I'm hanging up, then.</i>

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.590
Yeah... Take care.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.260
Wow... 39 degrees...

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.730
I hope Taichi's okay.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:54.810
Ayase...

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.970
Are you that dumb?

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:57.510
Huh?

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.150
Don't believe his lies!

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:03.630
I just asked my senpai in the Suihoku Society
who's helping at the qualifiers,

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.280
and he said his name's on the list!

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.530
<b><i>Call length 
0 min. 29 sec.</i></b>

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.630
Mashima's name is on the list 
of registered participants

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.290
in tomorrow's East Japan qualifiers!

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.200
<i>He's trying to get ahead of me!</i>

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.300
Oh, Taichi. How are you feeling?

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.540
Should you be up and walking around?

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:29.860
Yeah. I'm going out to study.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.430
Studying rather than forcing yourself
to go on a class trip?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.540
I think you made the right choice, personally.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.650
It's the autumn of your second year.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:42.400
If you're going to medical school, 
I'd like to see you go to KU or TU.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:44.280
I'll be back later.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.990
Fuchu City Katamachi Cultural Center

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.990
<b>Striving
 for the #1
recycling 
record in 
Japan!</b>

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.200
Sumire!

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:57.490
What's wrong with you, Sumire?

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:00.390
You were all fired up before,
 and today you're a total space case!

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:03.210
I know! It's 'cause Eyelashes-senpai 
is away on his class trip!

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:06.610
Shut up, you Four Tsukuba Stooges!

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:07.790
Tsukuba Stooges?!

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:08.360
Me, too?!

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.770
<i>Yeah, I </i>was<i> fired up.</i>

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.360
<i>I thought that was the only way I could 
get anywhere near Mashima-senpai.</i>

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:20.350
<i>But...</i>

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:25.730
<i>When I think about how he'll never even
see me if I can't compete at that level...</i>

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:34.220
<i>All I want is to be lovey-dovey 
with Mashima-senpai!</i>

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:37.750
Cheer up, Sumire! I'll put 
some fire back in you!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:38.610
No, I will!

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:39.370
I will!

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.340
<b>Favorite Cushion</b>

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:45.060
<i>H-He's here! The most fired-up guy of all!</i>

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.540
Where is Tsuboguchi-kun?

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.640
He said he wouldn't be coming today.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.060
He's at his school, preparing 
for the qualifiers on his own.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:55.860
How does he expect to prepare 
without playing me?!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:57.560
He's trying to run away!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.360
<i>I can understand how Tsuboguchi-san feels.</i>

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.830
<i>He'd be sucked into 
Dr. Harada's pace for sure.</i>

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:03.960
Tsukuba-kun!

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.820
You'll work just as well! 
Let's have a serious match!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:12.990
Only Class A players
 can be in the Master 
qualifiers

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.800
I-I'm still only in Class C!

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:12.990
It's fine! You're a Class C player 
who's destined for Class A!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.320
Huh?!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:23.020
Mashima-senpai, why are you here? 
What about your class trip?

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.800
I didn't feel well this morning, so I skipped it.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.930
What?!

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.210
But I feel better now,

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.850
so I'm here to practice.

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:37.810
<i>Practice?!</i>

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.710
<i>Why? Why?!</i>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.700
Right. I'm sure we can fit in three matches.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.150
Okay.

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:53.650
Play me as long as time allows, Eyelashes.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.180
Thank you for the game.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:04.180
What?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:09.010
The World of Nishijin-ori

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:09.010
<b>Tai</b>

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:09.010
President Mashima skipped the trip 
to be in the East Japan qualifiers?!

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.880
Shh!

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:15.360
<i>The class trip is the biggest event 
of high school life.</i>

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:20.290
<i>I thought he'd use this opportunity 
to get closer to Chihaya-chan.</i>

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.480
Like this...

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:24.730
All the Class 1 girls, in the depths of despair

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.310
<i>Chihaya-chan skipping the trip
would've been one thing,</i>

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.560
<i>but I never expected
President Mashima to skip it!</i>

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:30.240
I'm... I'm leaving, too.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.230
Huh?

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.850
Why am I in Kyoto while Taichi's in Tokyo?

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:39.880
Chihaya-chan!

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:43.750
I withdrew from the qualifiers, 
but he's in it? Why?

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.500
Why?

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:49.890
I never heard Taichi say
he wanted to be the Master!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.050
I don't understand!

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.520
Ayase, I sort of understand.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.580
Since he and I are in the same class,

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.980
I understand the time we have left.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.370
He wants to go to medical school,

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:18.020
so by this time next year,
 he'll be too busy for our club.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.950
And once he's in medical school, 
he won't have time for karuta at all.

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.530
If you really think about it,

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:28.070
this is his only chance to get 
as far as he can with karuta.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:31.220
<b>Women</b>

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:33.880
C'mon, Chi-chan, let's try out the sauna!

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.880
There's an outdoor bath over there, too!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.790
<i>I'm definitely in Kyoto.</i>

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.360
<i>Snowmaru
 Dorayaki 
New! Only
 in Kansai!</i>

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.660
<i>The moon looks so picturesque in the sky here.</i>

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:56.430
<i>I wonder where Shinobu-chan lives...</i>

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.410
<i>Snowmaru
 Dorayaki 
New! Only
 in Kansai!</i>

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.540
Wataya Arata Cell

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:22.620
Arata-niichan's not doing so well.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:26.600
He hasn't been for a while.
And tomorrow's the West Japan qualifiers...

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.990
Thank you very much.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.700
What's wrong, Arata?

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.570
Your swings are too wide.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:42.490
Even Taisuke could get under your 
hand to take cards that way.

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.420
You've been off your game 
since the Yoshino Tournament.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:46.860
You're not focusing.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:50.650
I can tell you're not 
envisioning your own victory.

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:56.340
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.050
<i>The qualifiers are tomorrow.</i>

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.520
<i>Why did I say that?</i>

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:11.070
Chihaya doesn't really belong 
to anyone, does she?

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:14.190
<i>Chihaya and Taichi are both my friends.</i>

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:16.450
<i>Why did I even think that?</i>

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:18.760
<i>Why aren't I the one</i>

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.650
<i>playing against Chihaya right now?</i>

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.400
<i>It was the same when Grandpa died,</i>

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.170
<i>and when I couldn't play karuta.</i>

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.340
<i>The time we spent together was my treasure.</i>

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:35.320
<i>What is this impatience I'm feeling?</i>

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.530
<i>Thinking about all this won't help.</i>

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.260
<i>I'm the one who has to work hard tomorrow.</i>

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:48.150
<i>Chihaya and Taichi's class trip ended up
being the day of the qualifiers.</i>

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.630
<i>I'll go to the West Japan Qualifier tomorrow</i>

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:53.620
<i>to become the Master.</i>

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:59.070
I can tell you're not 
envisioning your own victory.

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:05.970
Yuu?

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:08.510
What're you doing here?

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:10.800
You could've waited inside.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.780
Your parents aren't home.

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:16.570
Anyway, your family hasn't 
changed at all, huh?

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.940
Tomorrow is their son's big day,

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:21.460
and they're not making katsudon 
or katsu curry or anything?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:24.460
Oh... Yeah. They're the same as ever.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.470
Relatives are in town, so we're 
heading to a family restaurant. 

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.460
So I brought this.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:29.020
My mom made it.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:30.490
Thanks.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:34.220
Hey.

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:36.550
Why do you look so down?

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:37.380
Huh?

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:40.820
You've waited a whole 
year for the qualifiers.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:46.670
If you win, won't that attract new members
to your karuta club at school?

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:48.830
I...

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.440
wouldn't mind joining it.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.670
Wha—

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:56.280
What kind of puny reward 
for winning is that?

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.530
I don't need that!

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:58.850
Wow, rude!

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.920
You should know better than anyone!

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:04.140
I promised my grandpa that 
I'd become the Master!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:06.770
I don't need a reward 
for realizing my dream!

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:20.060
Well, you're the one standing here
shouting out the obvious.

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:22.120
Okay, good luck, then!

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.880
What's this?

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.570
Her mom didn't make this.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:36.520
<i>Yuu's the only one who would put 
katsudon and katsu curry together.</i>

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.300
Shinobu, could you get that?

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.460
Sure.

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:49.710
Y-You're still in your pajamas!

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:51.800
It's fine. I'll get the door.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.580
No, they're my street clothes. I'm good.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.000
W-Wait, Shinobu!

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:55.810
Coming!

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:03.060
Shinobu-chan, for this year...

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.400
Snowmaru
Dorayaki

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:08.150
Why don't we go make things
a little more exciting?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.520
<i>The day that a whole year,</i>

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:17.690
<i>or even longer, of hard work turns 
toward making dreams come true.</i>

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:22.600
<i>In the west,</i>

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:24.090
<i>and in the east,</i>

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.810
<i>a very special day is about to begin.</i>
